# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tarballs and zips are release *artifacts*, not sources. They are attached to
# the GitHub release, never committed. (The old data.zip / inode_usage.tar.gz
# workflow is exactly what this repo moved away from: the payload now lives in
# src/, lib/ and plugin/ in version control.)
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
SHA256SUMS
SHA256SUMS.asc
*.sig

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS AppleDouble / resource-fork junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The vendor tarball that shipped for roughly two years was built on a Mac with
# plain `tar`, so it carried ._install.json, ._meta.json and ._inode_usage.svg
# alongside the real files, plus com.apple.quarantine extended attributes.
# Those AppleDouble stubs got extracted onto the server and sat in the plugin
# directory forever. Never track them, and never build a release with them:
#
#   COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar --exclude='._*' --exclude='.DS_Store' \
#       -czf cPanel-Inodes-Usage-<version>.tar.gz <files>
#
# (On macOS use COPYFILE_DISABLE=1; GNU tar on Linux never creates these.)
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.AppleDouble
.AppleDesktop
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.VolumeIcon.icns
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.TemporaryItems
.apdisk
Icon?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS scratch files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
.idea/
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch space
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
/build/
/dist/
*.log
